# 11. SPINAL CORD — FUTURE TRANSPORT LAYER

The future architecture will introduce a separate communication and synchronization layer called the Spinal Cord.

Conceptually:

THE BRAIN:
- Owns memories.
- Understands relationships.
- Decides which context should be retrieved.
- Decides which information should be stored.
- Controls authorization and memory policies.

SPINAL CORD:
- Transports information.
- Handles communication protocols.
- Manages queues.
- Handles synchronization.
- Tracks delivery status.
- Handles retries and failures.
- Maintains transfer observability.

External AI entities:
- Claude.
- ChatGPT.
- Gemini.
- Local AI.
- Future providers.

Do not create an unnecessary transport subsystem now.

Instead, document clear boundaries and avoid coupling memory logic directly to future provider-specific communication code.

